# index.html contracts

Single HtmlService page. Tailwind via CDN, Inter font, emerald/slate/amber palette, `en-IN` currency. No build step and no extra framework. Theme control is fixed at the bottom left (`Light` / `Dark` / `System`, stored as `mf-matrix-theme`). `html.dark` restyles the chrome. Heat-map cell colors stay the same.

## Client state
`allFunds`, `currentDisplayFunds`, `top2FilterActive` (default **true**), `activeMetric` (`xirr` | `cagr`), sort field default `1Y` descending.

Data load: `google.script.run.getFundMatrixData`. Filters, Top 2, sort, and the metric switch stay in the browser. Changing SIP amount, SIP day, or dates calls `loadMatrixData` again.

## Filters and table
- Category, AMC, and Scheme are checkbox lists with Select All. Select All applies no restriction. The three lists intersect. Top 2 then keeps two schemes per remaining category by the active 1Y series.
- Tenure columns, in order: `5D` `15D` `1M` `3M` `6M` `9M` `1Y` `2Y` `3Y` `5Y` `7Y` `10Y` `12Y`. Header groups are Short and Long. `1Y` is emerald; `5Y` is amber.
- The SIP XIRR / Trailing CAGR switch re-renders tenure cells from `tenureXirr` or `tenureCagr`. Custom Range XIRR, SIP Corpus, Net Profit, and Absolute return do not follow the switch.
- Every metric column has a sort icon. Nulls sort last.
- Heat colors come from `getHeatmapStyle`. Corpus and Net Profit use the absolute-return color. NAV, units, and invested stay plain. Percents use `formatPct` (`+12.3%`).
- The matrix scrolls inside `.matrix-scroll`. Both header rows stay fixed. Columns through Fund Name (`#`, Code, Fund Name) stay fixed on horizontal scroll.
- Row up/down reorders the current view only.
